  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPACT: 23-0001164 Co-creation process for the design of an Integrated Water Resources Management program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPACT: 23-0001164 Proper water management is essential for the social and economic development of Mozambique, but it is at the same time one of the major national (and international) challenges, especially in view of climate change impacts and demographic and economic developments. As the Netherlands intends to continue its cooperation with Mozambique in IWRM, a new cooperation program for 2024-2027 is being prepared, which should create more synergy between the activities and to better harmonize the efforts of implementing partners (DNGRH, ARA-Centro and ARA-Norte). The IWRM program will consist of two phases: - The first phase (2023) is a co-creation process during which a Theory of Change will be developed and a full proposal for the program (current bemo). - In the second phase, the actual IWRM program will be implemented (2024-2027).</narrative>
  </description>
